    <!-- Visualization & Content Choices:
        - Firewall/IDS/IPS Definitions: Text + HTML/CSS diagram (Firewall at edge). Goal: Inform. Interaction: Static. Justification: Visual aid for core concept. Method: HTML/CSS.
        - IDS vs. IPS: Interactive HTML Table. Goal: Compare. Interaction: Hover/Click for details. Justification: Clear side-by-side comparison. Method: HTML/JS.
        - Types of Firewalls/IDS: Interactive HTML cards/list + HTML Table. Goal: Organize, Compare. Interaction: Click to expand. Justification: Manage extensive info. Method: HTML/JS.
        - Network Segmentation/DMZ: HTML/CSS/Canvas diagram. Goal: Illustrate. Interaction: Click to highlight zones. Justification: Visualizing complex topology. Method: HTML/JS/Canvas.
        - SIEM Integration: HTML/CSS/Canvas flow diagram. Goal: Illustrate. Interaction: Static. Justification: Show data flow. Method: HTML/CSS/Canvas.
        - Firewall Commands (Linux/Windows): Tabbed code blocks. Goal: Practical Info. Interaction: Tabs, Copy-to-clipboard. Justification: Easy access to commands. Method: HTML/JS.
        - No quantitative data suitable for Chart.js beyond simple conceptual comparisons if needed (e.g., feature counts), will prioritize HTML tables for comparisons.
        - CONFIRMING NO SVG/Mermaid. -->
    @{
        var numeros = new List<int> { 10, 20, 30 };
        var media = numeros.Average();
    }
    <p>Media: @media</p>
